    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nRight now, if you `cc` a file to try to rename it, it will actually delete the file and create a blank file with the new name. This can be shocking, especially if the file had untracked changes.\r\n\r\nUsing `C` works correctly, but it'd be nice to handle `cc` as well.",
