    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe whole idea of 'mini.files' file manipulation is to allow editing its buffers as regular text buffers as much as possible. This is powered by [having some concealed text in front of file basename](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/cff8f2bddbbc1093a9ffbf1122df918be5ff41d9/doc/mini-files.txt#L235-L244) which if deleted would mean that the file itself is assumed to later be deleted. As `cc` deletes whole line, this works as expected.\r\n\r\nTo mitigate shocking consequences, there is a confirm step which is *suggested* to be [read carefully](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/cff8f2bddbbc1093a9ffbf1122df918be5ff41d9/doc/mini-files.txt#L228).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
